  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "Given that \\(0\\lt a\\lt b\\lt c\\lt d,\\) which of the following is the largest?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\frac{a+b}{c+d}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\frac{a+d}{b+c}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\frac{b+c}{a+d}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\frac{b+d}{a+c}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\frac{c+d}{a+b}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "For positive fractions, increasing the numerator or decreasing the denominator increases the value. Here \\(c+d\\) is strictly larger than every numerator in choices A through D, while \\(a+b\\) is strictly smaller than every denominator in those choices.\n\nMore explicitly, let \\(N/M\\) be any of choices A through D. The given ordering implies \\(0<N<c+d\\) and \\(M>a+b>0\\), so\n\\[\n\\frac{N}{M}<\\frac{c+d}{M}<\\frac{c+d}{a+b}.\n\\]\nThus the largest expression is \\(\\frac{c+d}{a+b}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
